rashly:
Of poets are fresher than the world’s highways;
Forgive me that I rashly blew the dust
Which dims our hedges even, in your eyes,

rascal:
'Fo' he 'd even washed his face;
Would you b'lieve, de scan'lous rascal
Woke de birds erroun' de place?

rasp:
Was stormed and forced by the full rout of day:
The rasp of a saw, the fussy cluck and bray
Of hens, the wheeze of a pump, she needs must hear;
